I confess that “JavaScript” is unknown to me, though I take it to be a language for instructing calculating engines. By analogy, this function tests for a name, an `@` sign, and a domain:

```javascript
function isValidEmail(value) {
  return /^[^\s@]+@[^\s@]+\.[^\s@]+$/.test(value);
}
```

It is a modest rule rather than a complete treatment of every postal—or electronic—address.

I am unfamiliar with “Python,” which may be a newly devised system of mechanical instructions. The method is simply to compare a word with its reversal:

```text
function palindrome(word):
    return word == reverse(word)
```

Thus, “level” is a palindrome, whereas “house” is not.
